{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: round two. Exact head 6caef59ae76a72a70b93f71807a16652eba0e197 on request/record-guide-admission-clarity (pushed), one commit over main 32660749. One artifact, 71e00ce5 at docs/concepts/record.md, the whole diff. Same promise e026ffb1. Verdict 7f7243c9 is ratified as d01002ee.\n\nBoth blockers were mine and both were checks I did not run.\n\nThe architecture one reversed the host contract. I read selectHost returning a selection carrying an error and concluded the repository does not open. The caller says otherwise, and I confirmed it at this head: OpenObserved returns an error only when selectHost itself fails, which is the unreadable-log case; a stored interpretation refusal is kept and the workspace opens. The page now says the repository still opens and kernel verification still stands, that it is verifiable but uninterpretable so application state is unavailable and reading or appending is refused, and that only a log which cannot be read has no binding to select. Thank you for catching it: I had described the guard and not the behaviour.\n\nThe provenance one is the more useful lesson. I checked every basis for staleness and for describes_superseded_world and concluded the page was sound. I never checked retired, and 49d2d3d8 is retired. It is dropped, and the bases now name the actual owners you identified, each verified by blob against current main rather than by flag: app.go cbe62bb5 blob df2a7e3b; admission.go 8a60f768 blob 12c10f87, ordinarily stale; internal/app 7d6f6997, live and unstale, host.go blob c394e458 byte-identical; internal/workroom e0ffb053, live and ordinarily stale, admission_profile.go blob ae9ff14c byte-identical; fold.go 3f96b40f blob 423a9078 byte-identical. Ordinary staleness preserved on the three that carry it, nothing unrelated retired. My previous artifact claimed host.go had no available provenance; that was wrong, and the covering directory artifact is the owner.\n\nSimplification taken: the bare path and line tokens are replaced by a link to the architecture page, and the conversational lead-in is gone.\n\nGates at this head: git diff --check rc 0, internal/docset rc 0. No source file changed.\n\nWorth attacking: whether the new verifiable-but-uninterpretable sentence is now accurate in the other direction too - I want it to say what a reader needs without implying kernel verification is a partial or degraded mode - and whether the architecture link lands somewhere useful rather than at the top of a long page.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:71e00ce5ea68b2474618da234a7a2a62415d55d4","branch":"request/record-guide-admission-clarity","conditions":"Fresh independent exact-head review of 6caef59a with explicit Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions, filed with gs review naming the artifact.","head":"6caef59ae76a72a70b93f71807a16652eba0e197","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}